 "observations": [
  "body L1-L5: the end of the note a) on p. 20, ll. 22-30, begun on p. 177.",
  "body L1, L20, L29: the minus signs in the numerator of the third fraction of L1, in the denominator of the first fraction of L20 and in the numerator of L29 are printed as long dashes, the one in the denominator of the second fraction of L1 as a short dash; all are set as minus signs.",
  "body L5, L12: the R of the denominators is printed in another italic form, with an open bowl, like the P of the heads of the notes.",
  "body L18, L20: the bars of the middle fractions are printed broken.",
  "body L20: the numerator of the third fraction, «chorda ampl. solstit.», stands for the chord of the double arc HE, chorda 2 ampl. solstit., as in the third fraction of L18; the sines that follow in L23 (sin amplit.) hold for the double arc. Kept as printed.",
  "body L29: a short stroke after the full stop is not a sign.",
  "body L1-L33: the formulas are checked: with chorda 2a = 2 sin a and chorda 180° = 2R, Menelaus' theorem (Almagest II, 2 in L1 and II, 3 in L18) gives the sine forms and the rules of al-Battānī and of Ḥabash as printed, with the remarks on L20 and L33.",
  "body L33: the third rule of Ḥabash holds when tg is the ratio of sine and cosine; with the tangent of radius R, as in the tables, it reads sin ampl. = √((tg φ sin δ / R)² + sin² δ). Kept as printed.",
  "body L1: the first line stands lower than a line of text at the head of the page; the edition places it by the measured distance from the running head."
 ],
